      <div type="clause" n="39.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 39.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="516" ed="#liebermann"/>E s’il est en Denelae, seit forfait de sa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.9"/> laxlite, s’il alaier<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.15"/> ne se pot, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.2"/> il melz faire ne so[u]t<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.16"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="516" ed="#liebermann"/>In Danelahe erit in forisfactura de suo laslite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="39.2" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="270" ed="#robertson"/>E s'il est en Denelae seit forfait de sa laxlite, s'il alaier ne se pot que il melz faire ne so[u]t.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="516" ed="#liebermann"/>39, 2. Und wenn es im Dänen-Rechtsgebiet ist, sei er gestraft [Verwirkung?] in Höhe seiner Rechtsbruchbusse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_39-2.lnote.de1.c"/>, wenn er sich nicht eidlich entschuldigen kann, dass er nicht verstand besser zu urtheilen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">39, 2. And if it is in the Danish legal district, he shall be punished [forfeiture?] to the amount of his compensation for breach of law, unless he can excuse himself on oath that he did not understand how to judge better.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="271" ed="#robertson"/>And in the Danelaw he shall forfeit his lahslit, unless he can declare on oath that he did not know how to do better.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="516">II Cn 15.1[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 15, 1[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 270–271 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 516, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aleier <hi rend="italic">bessert MA.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">MA. corrects to aleier</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-2.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">solt <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">solt I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_39-2.lnote.de1.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Betrag wechselt; vgl.</hi> Northu. 51</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the amount varies; cf. Northu. 51</seg></note>
      </div>
